# A prompt, an answer or a /model written to a child that is exiting
# while it still holds the lease. Recipe: go/tests/model/README.md.
#
# A child leaves in two ways, and serve keeps its lease through both
# until the exit goroutine (internal/serve/supervisor.go start) has
# drained both pipes, reaped the process and run drop:
#   - Stop: Interrupt SIGINTs it; cmd/bough/main.go cancels the turn,
#     lets [cancelled]/[done] print (AwaitCancelled, up to 3 s), unmounts
#     every row and exits 130. That is the TAIL.
#   - a crash (SIGKILL, OOM, a panic): the process is gone at once, and
#     the lease is held only until the pumps see EOF and drop runs.
# Either way the process ends up exited with drop still to run: DEAD.
# ensure (supervisor.go) returns kids[id] in every one of these states:
# it never asks whether the child is on its way out.
#
# Where the code disagrees with the mapped model, the code wins:
#   - "stdin is never read again" after SIGINT is false. headlessPump
#     (plugins/ui/headless.go) reads stdin until the process exits. A
#     line that arrives before Unmount disposes hlInputs is submitted to
#     the loop, which may record its input and start a turn that Unmount
#     then kills (TailTake); one that arrives after spins in hlSubmit
#     until os.Exit and is gone (Exit). Either way POST /prompt said 200.
#     A /model read in the tail can still dispatch and record its
#     "model" entry (TailModelRead). A turn fast enough to finish inside
#     AwaitCancelled's 3 s is left out: llm-control holds every turn.
#   - "Answer in the window deletes the ask" happens only between the
#     SIGINT and "cancelled": the "cancelled" entry already deletes
#     s.asks, so an answer in the tail is ErrNoAsk. Before it, the pipe
#     is open, the write succeeds, Answer deletes the ask and the
#     cancelled turn never reads it (AnswerWhileSignalled).
#   - After a crash the pipe's read end is closed: a write is EPIPE, so
#     /prompt, /answer and /model are 500s, not 200s, and nothing is
#     saved or deleted (SetModel saves meta only after Send succeeds).
#     The page shows "Not sent"; its Retry respawns once drop has run.
#   - Stop on a line lost in the tail finds the child with unread set
#     and no turn (cancelled cleared inTurn): the interrupt is HELD, a
#     200, and the page sits on "Stopping" with the lost line unlanded.
#     Stop on a lost line after a /model respawned the child finds a
#     live idle child with nothing unread: the SIGINT makes it exit.
#   - A turn TailTake started does not stay open: the unmount cancels
#     it and records "cancelled", so Exit leaves it stopped, not
#     interrupted (found by the server walk).
#   - /think writes no history entry at all (plugins/commands/think.go),
#     so meta.Effort never survives any respawn, dying window or not.
#     Only /model is modelled; Effort is a finding, not a state.
#
# Fields (Session role):
#   child     the lease's process: alive | tail (SIGINT acted on,
#             cancelled recorded, exiting) | dead (exited, drop not yet
#             run) | none (dropped: the next ensure respawns with -r)
#   status    the turn as StatusOf reads it: idle | running | done |
#             stopped (cancelled) | interrupted (an open turn, no live
#             child). With an ask armed the row says needs-you; the
#             adapter maps that back to running.
#   sigint    a Stop's SIGINT is on its way to a running turn
#   ask       serve's armed ask (s.asks[id])
#   lostAnswer  a /answer was a 200 and the turn never read it (reset
#             when the next turn starts)
#   send      the page's current prompt: "" | accepted (200, not landed:
#             "Waiting") | failed (the "Not sent" row)
#   line      where the accepted prompt is: "" (landed or none) |
#             queued (a live child will read it) | tail (in the pipe of
#             an exiting child) | lost (its process is gone, unread)
#   model     the one /model switch, a -> b: a (meta a, runs a) |
#             queued (meta b, a live child will read it) | tail (meta b,
#             in an exiting child's pipe) | b (meta b, recorded: the
#             next child replays it) | lost (meta b, never recorded:
#             the next child runs a)
#   stopping  the page's Stop state: "" | stopping | failed ("Retry stop")
#   modelFirst  the /model line is ahead of the prompt line in the same
#             pipe. stdin is FIFO: a child reads the earlier line first.

role Session:
    action Init:
        # A session the page creates has a child from the start.
        self.child = "alive"
        self.status = "idle"
        self.sigint = False
        self.ask = False
        self.lostAnswer = False
        self.send = ""
        self.line = ""
        self.model = "a"
        self.stopping = ""
        self.modelFirst = False

    # ensure: a dropped lease respawns with -r, whose history store
    # closes a dangling turn as cancelled {interrupted: true}.
    atomic func ensure():
        if self.child == "none":
            self.child = "alive"
            if self.status == "interrupted":
                self.status = "stopped"

    # Send's write on whatever ensure handed back.
    atomic func deliver():
        if self.child in ("alive", "tail"):
            self.send = "accepted"
            self.line = "queued" if self.child == "alive" else "tail"
            if self.model in ("queued", "tail"):
                self.modelFirst = True
        else:
            # EPIPE: the process exited, drop has not run.
            self.send = "failed"

    # --- the person ---

    # Send with nothing live on the page (live = an unlanded send or a
    # running row; Settle runs before a person can type again).
    atomic action Prompt:
        require self.send == "" and self.status != "running" and self.stopping == ""
        self.ensure()
        self.deliver()

    # "Not sent" row, Retry: the same request again.
    atomic action Retry:
        require self.send == "failed"
        self.ensure()
        self.deliver()

    # "Not sent" row, Edit: the text goes back to the draft.
    atomic action Edit:
        require self.send == "failed"
        self.send = ""

    # The page still shows the lost prompt as "Waiting" (live), so the
    # person's next send goes out as a steer; with the lease dropped,
    # ensure respawns and the line runs as a prompt. It is the only way
    # the page's unlanded row is ever replaced.
    atomic action Resend:
        require self.send == "accepted" and self.line == "lost" and self.child == "none"
        self.ensure()
        self.deliver()

    # The model picker: POST /model writes "/model b" through Send (409
    # while an ask is armed) and saves meta.Model only if the write
    # succeeded. One switch, so the graph stays finite.
    atomic action SetModel:
        require self.model == "a" and not self.ask
        self.ensure()
        if self.child == "alive":
            self.model = "queued"
        elif self.child == "tail":
            self.model = "tail"
        # dead: EPIPE, a 500, meta unchanged.
        self.modelFirst = self.model in ("queued", "tail") and self.line not in ("queued", "tail")

    # POST /answer on the armed ask.
    atomic action Answer:
        require self.ask and self.child == "alive" and not self.sigint
        self.ask = False

    # The same answer after Stop's SIGINT, before "cancelled": the pipe is
    # open, the write is a 200 and Answer deletes the ask, but the turn
    # is being cancelled and never reads it.
    atomic action AnswerWhileSignalled:
        require self.ask and self.child == "alive" and self.sigint
        self.ask = False
        self.lostAnswer = True

    # Stop (Esc, the button, the palette), on a running row or an
    # unlanded send. A line a live child has not taken yet is the hold
    # stop_interrupt.fizz models, and is left out here.
    atomic action Stop:
        require (self.send == "accepted" or self.status == "running") and self.stopping != "stopping"
        require not (self.child == "alive" and self.line == "queued")
        self.stopping = "stopping"
        if self.child == "none":
            # 404 unknown session: "Retry stop".
            self.stopping = "failed"
        elif self.child == "alive":
            # A running turn, or a respawned idle child while the page
            # still shows a lost line: nothing unread, so a SIGINT.
            self.sigint = True
        # tail or dead: a held interrupt (unread, no turn) or a SIGINT to
        # an exiting process: 200, and nothing happens.

    # --- the child ---

    # The live child reads the prompt: the turn opens and the page lands
    # the input.
    atomic fair action Take:
        require self.line == "queued" and self.child == "alive"
        require not (self.model == "queued" and self.modelFirst)
        self.line = ""
        self.send = ""
        self.status = "running"
        self.lostAnswer = False

    # Not behind the prompt line, and not behind an answer the SIGINT
    # beat (that answer is read, and dropped, only after the cancel).
    atomic fair action ModelRead:
        require self.model == "queued" and self.child == "alive"
        require not (self.line == "queued" and not self.modelFirst)
        require not (self.lostAnswer and self.sigint)
        self.model = "b"
        self.modelFirst = False

    # The child reads its stdin long before a model request comes back
    # with a call: a /model written before the ask is read before it
    # arms. (Read after, the child would take the line as the answer.)
    atomic action Ask:
        require self.status == "running" and self.child == "alive" and not self.sigint
        require not self.ask and self.model != "queued"
        self.ask = True

    atomic action Finish:
        require self.status == "running" and self.child == "alive" and not self.sigint and not self.ask
        self.status = "done"

    # The SIGINT reaches the running turn: "cancelled" (which deletes the
    # armed ask), and the child starts its exit. A /model still in the
    # pipe is now read, if at all, by the tail.
    atomic fair action ChildSignal:
        require self.sigint and self.child == "alive"
        self.sigint = False
        if self.status == "running":
            self.ask = False
            self.status = "stopped"
            self.child = "tail"
            if self.model == "queued":
                self.model = "tail"
        else:
            # An idle child has no turn to cancel: it unmounts and exits
            # at once, with no tail, and a /model it had not read dies.
            self.child = "dead"
            if self.model == "queued":
                self.model = "lost"
            self.modelFirst = False

    # A tail line read before Unmount disposes hlInputs: the loop records
    # its input and starts a turn that the unmount kills.
    atomic action TailTake:
        require self.line == "tail" and self.child == "tail"
        require not (self.model == "tail" and self.modelFirst)
        self.line = ""
        self.send = ""
        self.status = "running"
        self.lostAnswer = False

    # A tail /model dispatched before the commands row unmounts: its
    # "model" entry is recorded, and the next child replays it.
    atomic action TailModelRead:
        require self.model == "tail" and self.child == "tail"
        require not (self.line == "tail" and not self.modelFirst)
        self.model = "b"
        self.modelFirst = False

    # Unmount done, exit 130. What the tail did not read dies with it. A
    # turn it took (TailTake) is cancelled by the unmount, which records
    # "cancelled" before the history row goes.
    atomic fair action Exit:
        require self.child == "tail"
        self.child = "dead"
        if self.status == "running":
            self.status = "stopped"
        if self.line == "tail":
            self.line = "lost"
        if self.model == "tail":
            self.model = "lost"
        self.modelFirst = False

    # SIGKILL, OOM or a panic.
    atomic action Crash:
        require self.child == "alive"
        self.child = "dead"
        self.sigint = False
        if self.line == "queued":
            self.line = "lost"
        if self.model == "queued":
            self.model = "lost"
        self.modelFirst = False

    # The exit goroutine: pumps drained, cmd.Wait, the "exit" event
    # (deletes the ask), drop. An open turn now reads interrupted.
    atomic fair action Drop:
        require self.child == "dead"
        self.child = "none"
        self.ask = False
        if self.status == "running":
            self.status = "interrupted"

    # --- the page ---

    # `stopping` clears once nothing is live.
    atomic fair action Settle:
        require self.send != "accepted" and self.status != "running" and self.stopping != ""
        self.stopping = ""

action Init:
    session = Session()

# Nothing is ever written to, or left waiting in, a process that has
# exited: its pipe is EPIPE, and what it had not read is lost.
always assertion NothingWaitsInAnExitedChild:
    return not (session.child in ("dead", "none") and (session.line in ("queued", "tail") or session.model in ("queued", "tail")))

# An armed ask belongs to a running turn of a child that can still read
# the answer, or to a crashed one whose exit event has not run yet.
always assertion AskOnlyInARunningTurn:
    return not (session.ask and (session.status != "running" or session.child in ("tail", "none")))

# An open turn with a live child is never read as interrupted: the
# respawn closes the dangling turn as stopped.
always assertion InterruptedHasNoLiveChild:
    return not (session.status == "interrupted" and session.child == "alive")

# Only an answer that raced Stop's SIGINT is lost: a live running turn
# that nobody stopped never had its answer swallowed.
always assertion AnswersLostOnlyToAStop:
    return not (session.lostAnswer and session.status == "running" and session.child == "alive" and not session.sigint)

# The lease is released: a tail exits, and a dead child is dropped.
always eventually assertion LeaseReleased:
    return session.child in ("alive", "none")

# A Stop's SIGINT is acted on (or dies with a crashed child).
always eventually assertion SignalActedOn:
    return not session.sigint

# A /model line is read or dies with its process: it never waits.
always eventually assertion ModelLineSettles:
    return session.model not in ("queued", "tail")

# The mapped claims the code breaks. Each was added as an assertion and
# fails; fizz's shortest counterexamples:
#
# ensure never hands out an exiting child:
#   always assertion NoDyingHandout: not (line == "tail" or model == "tail")
#   Prompt, SetModel, Take, Stop, ChildSignal (the /model still in the
#   pipe now waits on the tail); or a Prompt after ChildSignal: a 200
#   into a process that is unmounting.
#
# A 200 from /prompt means a process will read the line:
#   always assertion AcceptedIsRead: not (send == "accepted" and line == "lost")
#   Prompt, Crash. The tail loses it the same way: Prompt, Take, Stop,
#   ChildSignal, Prompt, Exit. Nothing tells the page: an exit is not an
#   input, so its "Waiting" row never lands.
#
# meta.Model is what the next live child runs:
#   always assertion ModelMatches: model != "lost"
#   SetModel, Crash; or through the tail: Prompt, Take, Stop, ChildSignal,
#   SetModel, Exit. meta says b; the -r child finds no "model" entry to
#   replay (cmd/bough/modelresume.go) and runs a.
#
# A 200 from /answer reaches the turn:
#   always assertion NoLostAnswer: not lostAnswer
#   Prompt, Take, Ask, Stop, AnswerWhileSignalled.
#
# Every accepted prompt eventually lands or becomes a visible failure:
#   always eventually assertion AcceptedLands: send != "accepted"
#   ... Prompt, Crash, Stop, Drop: "Waiting" forever unless the person
#   sends again (Resend is not fair).
#
# The page's "Stopping" always clears:
#   always eventually assertion StoppingClears: stopping != "stopping"
#   ... Prompt, Crash, Stop (a 200 from the dead child's lease: unread
#   and no turn, so held), Drop: the lost line keeps the page live, and
#   Stop stays disabled on "Stopping". After Drop, a Stop is a 404
#   ("Retry stop"), as mapped.
